{"version":2,"text":"Hashimoto’s Thyroiditis: Texts\n\nText D\n\nExam Date: 03 Jul 2018\n\nExam: ULTRASOUND THYROID\n\nClinical History\n? Thyroiditis.\n\nFindings\nThe thyroid gland is of normal size. The right lobe measured 52 x 11 x 14mm and left lobe 53 x 7 x 11mm.\nThe gland is generally heterogeneous but no discrete nodules or masses are seen. There is increased\nvascularity that is associated.\nNo retrosternal extension is seen and no masses are seen in the position of the parathyroid gland.\nThe capsule is intact.\n\nComment\nThere is evidence of a heterogeneous thyroid gland in keeping with\nthyroiditis. No dominant thyroid nodule is noted but a progress ultrasound would be useful to ensure small\nnodules do not change in size.\n\nEND OF PART A\n\nWebsite: http://oetonline.net.au\n\nThis resource was developed by OET Online\n\nPage 389\n\nEmail: info@oetonline.net.au","layout":{"version":1,"width":612.0,"height":792.0,"blocks":[{"text":"Hashimoto’s Thyroiditis: Texts","lines":[{"text":"Hashimoto’s Thyroiditis: Texts","x":0.3800455637254902,"y":0.029192739898989902,"width":0.27707026143790847,"height":0.02139035984848485,"confidence":1,"words":[{"text":"Hashimoto’s","x":0.3800455637254902,"width":0.11607189542483656,"confidence":1},{"text":"Thyroiditis:","x":0.5000292238562091,"width":0.10451960784313727,"confidence":1},{"text":"Texts","x":0.6084589624183007,"width":0.04865686274509798,"confidence":1}]}]},{"text":"Text D","lines":[{"text":"Text D","x":0.06567693627450981,"y":0.11117687373737373,"width":0.051156862745098036,"height":0.0183345946969697,"confidence":1,"words":[{"text":"Text","x":0.06567693627450981,"width":0.03393921568627451,"confidence":1},{"text":"D","x":0.10377497549019608,"width":0.01305882352941176,"confidence":1}]}]},{"text":"Exam Date: 03 Jul 2018","lines":[{"text":"Exam Date: 03 Jul 2018","x":0.06567693627450981,"y":0.16528070580808082,"width":0.18688039215686275,"height":0.018334593434343422,"confidence":1,"words":[{"text":"Exam","x":